# Avatar Kuruk (The Legend of Kuruk transformed): "Whenever you cast a spell, create a 1/1 colorless Spirit creature token ..." and "Exhaust -
# Waterbend {20}: Take an extra turn after this one." The Saga reaches chapter III on turn 5 and returns as Avatar Kuruk; Bot1 then casts
# two Black Lotuses and four Ornithopters (each cast makes a Spirit token: six). Bot2's own spell on turn 6 makes none ("Whenever YOU
# cast"). On turn 7 Bot1 casts another Ornithopter (a seventh Spirit) and pays {20} with seven mana (Island, three Moxen, one Lotus) and
# thirteen untapped artifacts and creatures tapped for waterbend (CR 701.67a), Avatar Kuruk itself among them, five Ornithopters and seven
# Spirits. The extra turn (CR 500.7) is turn 8, Bot1's again. There the {20} could be paid again - the second Lotus, the untapped
# Moxen, Island, Kuruk, the Ornithopters and Spirits, and the Ornithopter just cast, come to 22 - yet the exhaust ability is refused,
# because exhaust may be activated only once (CR 702.177a). The new Avatar Kuruk is a new object: no lore counters.

